course: dictionary
lesson: 13595
title: A health word: incontinence
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Incontinence is a medical word. It means not being able to control when you pass urine (wee) or poo. It is a health condition, not a choice. Context helps: «The doctor said the new medicine can help with incontinence.» A doctor is talking about a health problem, so incontinence must be a condition that medicine can treat.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Shops sell incontinence pads for people who need them.» Pads are things that help you stay dry and comfortable, so the sentence is about a need for extra care. Ask: what word would fit here? A health problem fits. A game or a holiday does not.
explain: This word is about private health, so we use it kindly and never as a joke. «Grandma has incontinence, so the family helps her stay clean and comfortable.» The sentence is caring and respectful. It shows that people with this condition deserve kindness, not laughter.
explain: Some older, formal writing uses the word in another way: a lack of self-control. When a word has two meanings, check which one fits the sentence around it, and if you are unsure, use a dictionary.
fact: Incontinence means not being able to control when you pass urine or poo.
fact: Incontinence is a medical condition, so it is a health problem, not a choice and not something to laugh at.
fact: Incontinence can affect babies, elderly people, and people who are ill.
fact: «Incontinence pads» are sold in shops to help people stay dry and comfortable.
fact: In an old, formal sense, incontinence means a lack of self-control.
exercise: «The doctor said the new medicine can help with incontinence.» What is incontinence in this sentence? | A type of exercise for the legs | A sweet treat given after a check-up | A kind of bandage for a cut | *A health condition where you cannot control when you pass urine or poo
exercise: «Shops sell incontinence pads for people who need them.» What are incontinence pads for? | Keeping the sun out of your eyes | Playing games in the park | *Helping people stay dry and comfortable | Washing the dishes
exercise: In old, formal writing, incontinence can mean something different. What does it mean then? | A happy mood | Strong muscles | Good manners | *A lack of self-control
test: «Grandad has incontinence, so we are kind and private about it.» What is the best way to treat someone with incontinence? | Tell everyone in the class about it | Laugh so they feel better | *Be kind and private, with respect | Ignore them completely
test: Which statement about incontinence is true? | It is a choice that people make | It is a kind of food | It only happens to people who have done something wrong | *It is a medical condition that can affect babies, older people, and people who are ill
exam: «The nurse spoke quietly and kindly about incontinence.» What does this sentence show about the word? | It is a game played with a ball | It is a silly joke to tell at lunch | It is a sport for the winter | *It is a private health matter that deserves a kind, careful response
